   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing critical gaps in HIV Prevention, Treatment, Care and Support in Zimbabwe - Zimbabwe (01-Jan-2014-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Zimbabwe)This program has the following goals: Reduce % of infants born to women with HIV who are infected from 18% in 2010 to 7% in 2013 to 4% by 2015 to 2% by 2017.  Reduce HIV related mortality from 25,955 (2012),  to 14,050 for adults  (15-49) and 4,801  (2012)  to 2,373 for children by 2017  (2015 HIV Etimates).  Reduced new HIV infections in adults (15-49) from 1.09 % in 2012 to 1.03%  in 2013; 2014  projected to 0.95%; 2015 to  0.88%;  2016 to 0.8% and 2017 to 0.6% (2015 Estimates HIV Estimates ). The objectives of this program are: To improve the timeliness and completeness of reports to 95% by 2016.  To increase provision of HTC to 2,777,000 per year by end of 2016).  To increase the health worker retention to 94% (Doctors) and 98% (Nurses) by 2016.  To increase the number and coverage of male circumcised to 1,300,000 (80%) by end of 2017.  To increase the number of HIV pregnant women on ART provision to 63,578 (90% of 70,642) in 2017.  To increase the number of PLHIV receiving ART to 1,092,944 for adults and Children  in 2017.  To scale-up rollout of ePMS to 534 health facilities by 2016.  To support adoption of safer sexual practices and uptake of HIV prevention services to key populations</narrative>
  </description>
